cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "ZeroMiss: a validated missile-guidance interception simulator"
abstract: >-
  An interception simulator for the mathematics of pursuit. A Python
  source-of-truth engine implements pursuit, PPN, TPN, APN and ZEM-optimal
  guidance over a fixed-step RK4 integrator, with seeker lag, noise, field of
  view and loss of lock, airframe acceleration limits and autopilot lag, and
  vectorised Monte-Carlo campaigns for probability of kill and CEP. Correctness
  is demonstrated rather than claimed: the suite reproduces known results
  (zero miss for N >= 3 against a non-manoeuvring target, heading-error washout,
  the Zarchan step-manoeuvre miss curve, APN cancelling a lag-induced step miss
  that TPN cannot, and fourth-order RK4 convergence). The guidance core is
  independently re-implemented in TypeScript, MATLAB/Octave, C++ and a Simulink
  block diagram, and continuous integration asserts the browser twin reproduces
  every Python reference run to within 0.1 per cent.
type: software
